WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.444 --> 00:00:08.227
The children watched Mademoiselle and Lord Yalding walk away.

2
00:00:08.327 --> 00:00:15.091
"So the caretaker is Lord Yalding!"

3
00:00:15.111 --> 00:00:15.411
said Jimmy.

4
00:00:15.451 --> 00:00:19.273
"And Mademoiselle is his friend."

5
00:00:33.032 --> 00:00:34.493
"She's not his friend!"

6
00:00:34.994 --> 00:00:36.174
Mabel said scornfully.

7
00:00:36.194 --> 00:00:41.699
"She's the lady he wanted to marry, but his uncle wouldn't let him.

8
00:00:42.179 --> 00:00:44.280
She's the one who was sent to the convent!"

9
00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:49.824
"And now the ring has brought them together," said Kathleen.

10
00:00:49.845 --> 00:00:54.688
"I wonder if they'll be married tomorrow," said Mabel.

11
00:00:54.708 --> 00:00:58.451
"Wouldn't it be fun if we were bridesmaids?"

12
00:00:58.931 --> 00:00:59.692
said Kathleen.

13
00:01:02.096 --> 00:01:04.618
"I think Mademoiselle is very lucky."

14
00:01:05.178 --> 00:01:05.999
Mabel sighed.

15
00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:09.841
Mademoiselle was also very happy.

16
00:01:12.303 --> 00:01:15.525
Years ago her guardian had put her in the convent.

17
00:01:16.926 --> 00:01:21.109
He'd said he didn't want her to lose her fortune by marrying a poor lord.

18
00:01:22.991 --> 00:01:26.033
But he had really wanted her fortune for himself.

19
00:01:27.514 --> 00:01:30.676
So he'd stolen all her money and run off to South America.

20
00:01:32.552 --> 00:01:34.433
And she'd been left with nothing.

21
00:01:37.274 --> 00:01:39.775
Mademoiselle had had to work in order to live.

22
00:01:40.835 --> 00:01:45.377
She'd taken the job at Kathleen's school because it was near Lord Yalding's home.

23
00:01:46.538 --> 00:01:50.679
She still loved him even though she thought he didn't love her anymore.

24
00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:55.721
She didn't know that he had been looking for her all this time.

25
00:02:00.383 --> 00:02:03.761
The day after the picnic, Lord Yalding came to the school.

26
00:02:04.781 --> 00:02:09.503
He took everyone back to the castle in a wagon pulled by two fine horses.

27
00:02:12.344 --> 00:02:14.585
The children wanted to explore the castle.

28
00:02:17.406 --> 00:02:22.228
Mabel showed them all the secret doors and secret passages and secret stairs.

29
00:02:29.891 --> 00:02:31.392
They ate lunch in the great hall.

30
00:02:33.532 --> 00:02:36.194
It was where Mabel had first served them bread and cheese.

31
00:02:37.696 --> 00:02:41.619
This time they ate a real meal served on silver dishes.

32
00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:47.363
Gerald raised his glass of lemonade for a toast: "To Lord and Lady Yalding."

33
00:02:50.746 --> 00:02:53.929
Mademoiselle's eyes were bright with tears of happiness.

34
00:02:53.949 --> 00:02:59.113
"And by the way Gerald said to Lord Yalding.

35
00:02:59.133 --> 00:03:03.476
"I know you don't believe in the ring, but we do.

36
00:03:04.037 --> 00:03:04.977
May we have it back?"

37
00:03:06.638 --> 00:03:08.418
Lord Yalding handed him the ring.

38
00:03:10.159 --> 00:03:14.221
But Lord Yalding and Mademoiselle could not be completely happy yet.

39
00:03:15.601 --> 00:03:19.263
They had found each other, but they could not afford to live in the castle.

40
00:03:19.623 --> 00:03:21.704
They talked of renting it to someone rich.

41
00:03:22.904 --> 00:03:25.125
But they didn't know anyone with enough money.

42
00:03:25.145 --> 00:03:28.767
"I have an idea," said Jimmy.

43
00:03:28.787 --> 00:03:31.808
"Why don't you sell your jewels?"

44
00:03:33.616 --> 00:03:34.317
"What jewels?"

45
00:03:34.917 --> 00:03:35.858
said Lord Yalding.

46
00:03:35.878 --> 00:03:38.060
"I don't have any jewels."

47
00:03:40.421 --> 00:03:43.984
"I mean the ones in the paneled room with the stars on the ceiling.

48
00:03:44.324 --> 00:03:47.266
There are shelves and shelves of beautiful family jewels.

49
00:03:47.787 --> 00:03:51.750
You could sell them and "Oh no!"

50
00:03:52.190 --> 00:03:53.231
cried Mademoiselle.

51
00:03:53.251 --> 00:03:55.552
"Don't sell the family jewels."

52
00:03:55.572 --> 00:04:00.296
"There aren't any jewels, my lady," said Lord Yalding.

53
00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:04.741
"Oh yes, there are," said Mabel.

54
00:04:04.761 --> 00:04:06.022
"Come and see."

55
00:04:06.042 --> 00:04:11.886
"Let's see what Mabel shows us," said Mademoiselle.

56
00:04:11.906 --> 00:04:14.807
"At least it will be amusing."

57
00:04:16.908 --> 00:04:19.750
"It will be amusing," Jimmy promised.

58
00:04:22.091 --> 00:04:25.493
Gerald and Kathleen stayed behind to help Mabel's aunt clean up.

59
00:04:27.374 --> 00:04:29.896
So Jimmy and Mabel led the way to the treasure room.

60
00:04:31.772 --> 00:04:34.713
Mademoiselle and Lord Yalding followed, holding hands.

61
00:04:34.733 --> 00:04:39.914
"It's much safer to walk hand in hand," Lord Yalding said.

62
00:04:39.934 --> 00:04:43.735
"You never know what will happen with these children."

63
00:04:45.376 --> 00:04:48.617
Lord Yalding did not know what to think as he followed the children.

64
00:04:49.677 --> 00:04:51.657
They seemed to believe in the magic ring.

65
00:04:52.738 --> 00:04:55.538
They also seemed to believe the strange stories they told.

66
00:04:57.479 --> 00:05:01.440
When they reached the treasure room, Mabel said, "Now you'll see."

67
00:05:04.488 --> 00:05:05.930
The others gathered around her.

68
00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:09.835
"There's a secret button here somewhere."

69
00:05:10.335 --> 00:05:12.358
Mabel's fingers fumbled for the button.

70
00:05:12.378 --> 00:05:15.922
"Where?" said Lord Yalding.

71
00:05:15.942 --> 00:05:19.806
"Here," Mabel said impatiently.

72
00:05:19.826 --> 00:05:22.530
"Only I can't find it!"
